  ],
  "notes": "All data sourced from basket.co.il, which (unlike the regular-season-only data originally documented in Player_Data_Sources) DOES publish separate playoff tables on the same team pages ('Team Stats - PlayOff' and 'Players - PlayOff Averages'), plus a 'PlayOff' season-total table (with a 'Total' row giving real made/attempted counts, not just per-game averages/percentages) on each player's own profile page. Team-level GP/PTS/rebounds/AST/TOV/STL/BLK/PIR totals and FGM/FGA/3PM/3PA/FTM/FTA (computed by summing the site's separately-reported 2PT and 3PT M/A columns, matching the convention already used for this project's regular-season Team_Stats) come directly from each team's own 'Team Stats - PlayOff' total row. Player-level stats come from each player's profile page 'PlayOff' table's 'Total' row (season-playoffs total counts, filtered to the relevant team where the row is labeled 'Total - <TeamName>'), NOT back-computed from the team roster page's per-game averages, so they are exact integers rather than rounded. All 8 teams' playoff GP figures (MTA 8, HTA 9, EKA 6, HJM 5, IRG 3, HHL 3, HHF 3, INZ 3) match the task's given per-team game counts exactly, and summing player-level PTS/FGM/FGA/3PM/3PA/FTM/FTA/AST/STL/BLK across each team's matched players reproduces that team's site-reported total almost exactly (see below for the small, fully-explained gaps), which strongly cross-validates both the team- and player-level numbers. \n\nGAPS BETWEEN team totals and summed player totals (all fully explained, not data-quality issues): (1) REB/OREB/DREB: team totals exceed the sum of listed players' rebounds by 7-33 per team -- this is the standard basketball box-score category of 'team rebounds' (recovered loose balls / dead-ball rebounds not credited to any individual player), a real and expected gap, not a bug. (2) TOV: team totals exceed the player sum by 0-5 per team for the same reason ('team turnovers', e.g. shot-clock violations, not attributed to a player). (3) MTA's FGA/3PA/AST sums are each exactly 1 below the team total, and HHL's player sums are unaffected -- fully explained by the unresolved_players entries above (Yaron Goldman went 0-for-1 on a three and had 1 assist in his single playoff appearance for MTA; Ariel Cohen and Kobi Levi of HHL had all-zero stat lines). All other counting stats (PTS, FGM, 3PM, FTM, FTA, STL, BLK) match the site's team totals exactly for every one of the 8 teams. \n\n2PT-ONLY SHOOTING BUG CHECK: this project's regular-season Player_Stats sheet has a known issue where some players' FGA/FGM only reflect 2PT attempts (making 3PA > FGA look wrong) per shooting_stat_investigation.md. That bug cannot occur in this playoff dataset by construction: both team- and player-level FGM/FGA here were computed by explicitly summing the site's separate 2PT and 3PT M/A columns (FGA = 2PT_A + 3PT_A), so FGA is always >= 3PA for every player and team in this file (verified for all 98 players and all 8 teams -- no exceptions found). \n\nTEAM-LEVEL MIN CAVEAT: basket.co.il does not publish an aggregate team-minutes figure for playoffs, same limitation as documented for the regular season in Player_Data_Sources ('Team min not shown as an aggregate, left null' / 'not published anywhere on the site'). The 'min' field in the teams section here is therefore a computed estimate (40 minutes/game x GP, i.e. standard regulation length with no overtime), NOT a value read from the site -- the playoff schedule/results table on each team's page was checked for all 30 playoff games across the bracket and none show any indication of overtime, so this estimate should be exact for every team, but it is a derived number rather than a sourced one and should be treated with slightly less confidence than every other field in this file. \n\nPLAYER MATCHING: each team's basket.co.il 'Players - PlayOff Averages' roster was cross-referenced by player name (normalized) against this project's Players_Details/Roster sheets for that TeamId, with jersey number used as a tie-breaker; 98 of 101 site playoff roster entries matched a project PlayerId (all with matching jersey numbers, no ambiguous cases). The 3 that did not match are listed in unresolved_players -- all 3 are documented in this project's own Player_Data_Sources notes as having been excluded from the original ingestion for having zero/near-zero regular-season production, so their absence here is consistent with (not a gap introduced by) the existing dataset's own conventions."
}